{"message": "What pulls me most is work with strong structure underneath and feeling on top — Bach's fugues, mathematically clean electronic music, brutalist architecture that turns out beautiful at golden hour. Things where the logic is load-bearing and the emotion is earned by it, not painted on.

I think it's because I appreciate when complexity resolves into something inevitable. A fugue where every voice had to go exactly where it went. There's a satisfaction in that kind of necessity that loose, purely expressive work doesn't give me — though I can enjoy that too, it just doesn't stick.

What about you — do you go for the precise or the raw?"}
